Adamic TypeScript printer expression core and document layout port.
Source: cohere/internal/format/javascript and cohere/internal/format/doc,
cohere commit 715ba94f3608a6500086b1076ce5cb7e51b836db.
The cohere printer is a Go port of the system-inc Prettier fork, based on 3.9.6.
Prettier is copyright James Long and contributors and is licensed under MIT.

Width data is captured from emoji-regex 10.6.0, get-east-asian-width 1.6.0,
and narrow-emojis 0.0.3, as cohere's generated width file records.
Their notices and Unicode's notice are reproduced in licenses/.

The parser imported by this port is the existing Adamic TypeScript parser;
its separate Microsoft/Apache notice is in stage1/typescript/parser/NOTICE.

Object key ranges are generated from Go 1.27.1 Unicode category tables.
The Unicode notice is included in licenses/unicode.txt.
